      "derivation": "VerifyLeader's API promises leadership assurance for preventing stale data after leadership loss. AddNonvoter explicitly assigns no vote and excludes election and commitment participation; ServerSuffrage identifies voting eligibility. These declarations do not explicitly specify the VerifyLeader algorithm. The bounded eligibility requirement is derived by combining those interface responsibilities with the implementation's use of a voter-only quorum threshold: support from a participant outside that electorate cannot establish the corresponding voter quorum. Actual code separately shows registration with every replication worker and identity-free positive vote aggregation. This is an attributable local requirement and a concrete suspicion, not a conclusion that leadership was lost.",
